# Tracer: anonymous functions retain and consume their verifier-owned WD scope.
#
# Before (Litex verified, but To-Lean did not work):
# fn(x R) R {x} = fn(y R) R {y}
# forall a R:
#     fn(x R) R {x}(a) = fn(x R) R {x}(a)
# Former behavior: emission stopped at an unsupported AnonymousFunction object;
# the checked x-in-R binder premise and return-closure fact never reached a
# Litex.functionObject constructor.
#
# Now (verified and compiled by the focused Rust/Mathlib gates):
fn(x R) R {x} = fn(y R) R {y}

forall a R:
    fn(x R) R {x}(a) = fn(x R) R {x}(a)
# Current behavior: each anonymous occurrence owns one binder scope, one exact
# return-closure route, one functionObject, and one checked FnSet membership;
# an applied anonymous head reuses that membership to construct Applicable.
#
# Boundary: fn(x R) N {x} remains rejected because x-in-N is not proved. A
# body whose target Object term itself needs local WD proofs, such as x + 1,
# still requires the proof-aware function-body ABI decision recorded in the
# To-Lean status ledger.
# Evidence:
# target/release/litex -compact -isolated -runner -f examples/05_compiler_interop/compile_to_lean_anonymous_function.lit
# cargo test --release anonymous_function_emits_checked_constructor_and_head_application -- --nocapture
# LITEX_LEAN_PROJECT=lean cargo test --release anonymous_function_compiles_with_mathlib -- --ignored --nocapture
